     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":4,\"rationale\":\"Block appServer:lateralMovement, jumpHost:lateralMovement, serviceAccount:privilegeEscalation and printServer:lateralMovement; three blocks cannot work. Case 1, appServer is not blocked: it is reachable via memoryDump, which comes straight from entries. It then feeds vaultRead, codeRepo and dbReplica directly, so each of those (or something equivalent) must be blocked. shareMount is still reachable through jumpHost, which comes from configSecret or dbLogin, so that is at least 4. Blocking all of appServer's parents instead (memoryDump, apiToken, ssoLogin) costs 3, and jumpHost still needs a fourth. Case 2, appServer is blocked: three paths remain. configSecret leads to jumpHost and then shareMount. memoryDump leads to printServer and then dbReplica. ssoLogin together with vpnSession leads to serviceAccount and then codeRepo. These paths share no blockable node, so 3 more blocks are needed, giving 4. The proposed set of 4 works: vaultRead's sources are all gone (hypervisor and secretsManager both need jumpHost), shareMount loses jumpHost and localAdmin, codeRepo loses both parents, and dbReplica loses appServer, hypervisor and printServer.\"}"
    }
   ],
